*     FAP                                                                       
       LBL     ILOG                                                     ILOG0000
       COUNT   50                                                       ILOG0001
*      UNIVERSITY OF CHICAGO COMPLEX LOGARITHM SUBROUTINE               ILOG0002
*              REAL AND IMAGINARY ARGUMENTS ARE NORMAL, FLOATING POINT  ILOG0003
*              NUMBERS STORED IN CELLS 32767 AND 32766 RESPECTIVELY.    ILOG0004
*              ANSWER COMES OUT IN SAME CELLS                           ILOG0005
*              CALLING SEQUENCE                                         ILOG0006
*                            TSX   $ILOG,4                              ILOG0007
*              IMAGINARY ANSWER WILL BE BETWEEN + AND -PI               ILOG0008
*              IF X = Y = 0, EXECUTION IS TERMINATED BY EXEM            ILOG0009
       ENTRY   ILOG                                                     ILOG0010
  ILOG SXA     X4,4          SAVE INDEX REGISTER                        ILOG0011
       DLD     4)-1          IF THE CHARACTERISTIC OF Y MINUS THE       ILOG0012
       SSP                   CHARACTERISTIC OF X IS GREATER THAN OR     ILOG0013
       LRS     0             EQUAL TO 33 OCTAL, THE IMAGINARY PART OF   ILOG0014
       SUB     C1            THE ANSWER IS SIMPLY (SIGNY)*PI/2          ILOG0015
       TLQ     CKT3                                                     ILOG0016
       CLA     4)-1          IMAGINARY CIRCUIT                          ILOG0017
       NZT     4)            SPECIAL TREATMENT IF REAL ARGUMENT = 0     ILOG0018
       TRA     CKT2                                                     ILOG0019
       FDP     4)              =ATAN(Y/X)                               ILOG0020
       XCA                                                              ILOG0021
       TSX     $ATAN,4                                                  ILOG0022
       LDQ     4)                                                       ILOG0023
       TQP     ANGLOK                                                   ILOG0024
       TPL     *+3           SET IN                                     ILOG0025
       FAD     PI              PROPER QUADRANT                          ILOG0026
       TRA     *+2                                                      ILOG0027
       FSB     PI                                                       ILOG0028
       FRN                                                              ILOG0029
ANGLOK STO     BUF                                                      ILOG0030
       TSX     $IABS,4       REAL CIRCUIT                               ILOG0031
       CLA     -1                                                       ILOG0032
       TSX     $LOG,4          =LOG(X**2+Y**2)**1/2                     ILOG0033
       LDQ     BUF                                                      ILOG0034
       XCA                                                              ILOG0035
       DST     4)-1                                                     ILOG0036
    X4 AXT     **,4          RESET INDEX                                ILOG0037
       TRA     1,4           RETURN                                     ILOG0038
  CKT2 TZE     GOOF          IF BOTH PARTS ARE = 0, AN ANSWER IS NOT    ILOG0039
  CKT3 LDQ     4)-1          POSSIBLE, SO ONE MUST EXIT                 ILOG0040
       CLA     PIOV2                                                    ILOG0041
       LLS     0                                                        ILOG0042
       TRA     ANGLOK                                                   ILOG0043
  GOOF LDI     *+2           LEAVE IF BOTH ARGUMENTS ARE ZERO           ILOG0044
       TRA*    $(EXEM)                                                  ILOG0045
       PZE     6,7,X4                                                   ILOG0046
    PI OCT     202622077325                                             ILOG0047
 PIOV2 OCT     201622077325                                             ILOG0048
    C1 OCT     33000000000                                              ILOG0049
   BUF BSS     1                                                        ILOG0050
    4) EQU     -1                                                       ILOG0051
       END                                                              ILOG0052
